---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const pageTitle = 'Privacy Policy';
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle}>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <section class="mx-auto my-24 max-w-3xl px-5 md:my-36" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="mb-8 flex flex-col items-center">
        <h1
          class="font-clash-display-bold text-center text-4xl leading-tight text-slate-800 md:text-6xl"
        >
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
      </div>
      <div class="text-sm leading-8 text-slate-700 md:text-lg">
        <p class="mb-2 text-base text-slate-500">Last updated: December 2024</p>

        {/* Preamble */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">Preamble</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          This Privacy policy applies to the website <a
            href="https://www.air360.io/"
            class="text-blue-600 underline">https://www.air360.io/</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Privacy of our clients, partners and suppliers as well as your privacy, as users of the
          website
          <a href="https://www.air360.io/" class="text-blue-600 underline">
            https://www.air360.io/
          </a>, is key for us. The purpose of this privacy policy is to provide you with information
          concerning how we collect Personal information when you use this website, how we use and
          process collected information; and choices you may have about the ways we collect, process
          and use that information. Our goal is not only to comply with applicable data protection
          and privacy laws (including the Regulation EU 2016/679 of April 27, 2016, also known as
          General Data Protection Regulation - GDPR), but also to minimize the process of that
          Personal information.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          “Personal information” means in a nutshell information that identifies you personally,
          directly or indirectly, either alone or in combination with other information.
        </p>

        {/* Which information do you collect? */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">
          Which information do you collect?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          The Personal information we collect includes, but is not limited to, your name, email
          address, IP address, phone number and other information about you voluntarily submitted to
          verify who you are or to prevent fraud. If you contact us, we may collect additional
          Personal information which you knowingly and voluntarily provide through your contact with
          us.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We furthermore collect information that is sent to us automatically by your web browser,
          which may include, without limitation, information that does not identify you personally
          (such as the date and time of your visit). The information we receive in this manner
          depends on the settings on your web browser. If you have created a user identity on one of
          our interactive services, we may use browser information provided by your browser to
          information that identifies you personally and use it for the purposes described below.
          Please refer to the settings of your web browser if you want to learn what information
          your browser sends or how to change your settings.
        </p>

        {/* Cookies or not cookies */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">Cookies or not cookies</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Consistent with our vision of data analytics and our desire to minimize the use of
          personal data, the air360.io site is cookie-free.
        </p>

        {/* Social Plugins */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-8 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">Social Plugins</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Our website may use social plugins (“plugins”) of some social networks such as Instagram,
          X (ex-Twitter) or LinkedIn.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          These plugins can be recognized by their famous logos appearing on Air360.io website. As
          soon as a web page is being accessed which contains such a plugin, your browser will
          establish a direct connection with the servers of the social media. The content of the
          plugin will usually be communicated directly from the relevant social media to your
          browser and embedded in the web page. We therefore have no influence on the amount of data
          the relevant social media obtains through these plugins.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We are not acquainted with the purpose and extent of the data collection as well as any
          further processing and use of the data by the relevant social media.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          <a href="https://developers.facebook.com/docs/plugins/page-plugin" class="text-blue-600"
            >https://developers.facebook.com/docs/plugins/page-plugin
          </a>
        </p>

        {/* Facebook */}
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-8 text-lg font-bold text-slate-800">Facebook</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Our website may use social plugins (“plugins”) of the social network facebook.com which is
          operated by Facebook Inc., 1601 S. California Ave, Palo Alto, CA 94304, USA.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          These plugins can be recognized by one of the Facebook logos (white “f” on a blue tile or
          a “thumbs-up” sign) or are marked as “Facebook Social Plugin”. A list of Facebook social
          plugins with illustrations is available on:
        </p>

        {/* X (ex-Twitter) */}
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-8 text-lg font-bold text-slate-800">X (ex-Twitter)</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Our websites may use social plugins from the social network twitter.com operated by
          Twitter Inc., 795 Folsom St., Suite 600, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          These plugins are identifiable by their “X” logo (white bird on blue square).
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          In particular, they allow you to share the content of our website with your “X” contacts.
        </p>

        {/* Instagram */}
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-8 text-lg font-bold text-slate-800">Instagram</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Our websites may use plugins from the Instagram social network operated by Instagram LLC,
          1601 Willow Rd Menlo Park CA 94025 USA.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          These plugins are identifiable by their Instagram logo (minimalist camera).
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          In particular, they allow you to share the content of our website with your Instagram
          contacts.
        </p>

        {/* LinkedIn */}
        <h3 class="mb-2 mt-8 text-lg font-bold text-slate-800">LinkedIn</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Our websites may use LinkedIn social network plugins operated by LinkedIn, 1000 W. Maude
          Ave, Sunnyvale, CA 94085, USA.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          These plugins are identifiable by their LinkedIn logo (letter L in a blue box).
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">They allow you to share content of our website on this social network.</p>

        {/* What use are you making of this information? */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">
          What use are you making of this information?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          We may use Personal information collected by us for the following purposes:
        </p>
        <ul class="mb-6 ml-6 list-disc space-y-3 text-slate-700">
          <li>to contact you if you have requested information or communication from us;</li>
          <li>
            to determine the country in which you are located for potential compliance purposes and
            for security, anti-piracy, and fraud prevention purposes;
          </li>
          <li>
            to help verify that existing personal information about you, in our possession, is
            accurate and complete;
          </li>
          <li>
            to provide you with product updates and upgrades, special offers, pricing information,
            newsletters, and other information, either on our own behalf or in some cases on behalf
            of a partner or client acting as their agent, where you have consented to receive it;
          </li>
          <li>
            to undertake any other promotional activity in the case you have consented to receiving
            and participating to such promotional or communication activity;
          </li>
          <li>to verify compliance with applicable laws, rules and regulations;</li>
          <li>
            to provide you, to the extent permitted by law, with a personalized user experience; for
            you to potentially establish an account for future login, if you have consented to the
            creation of such an account;
          </li>
          <li>
            to provide you with effective user service (which may to the extent and in a manner
            permitted by applicable law.)
          </li>
        </ul>

        {/* What are my choices */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">What are my choices</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We respect your right to make choices about the ways we collect and use Personal
          information about you. We generally ask you to indicate your choices at the time and on
          the page where you provide your personal information.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          When you provide personal information, we may offer you a choice as to whether you would
          like to receive further communications from us and/or from our partners, such as
          communications related to updates, upgrades, special offers and pricing. You have the
          right to withdraw your consent at any time. If you decide you no longer want to receive
          promotional messages from us, you may let us know via the contact form on our website (<a
            href="https://www.air360.io/"
            class="text-blue-600 underline">https://www.air360.io/</a
          >) or by email at <a href="mailto:privacy@air360.io" class="text-blue-600 underline"
            >privacy@air360.io</a
          >. Please specify which consent you are revoking in your email to us. Please note,
          however, if you give us permission to add your contact information to the Merchant’s
          mailing list and later withdraw your permission, you will have to contact the Merchant (or
          use the “opt-out” provided in the emails the Merchant sends you) to have your name removed
          from the Merchant’s mailing lists.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We may use third party service providers to serve ads on our behalf across the Internet,
          and sometimes on this website. Therefore, you may receive communications, including
          emails, from our partners but only if you have given your prior explicit consent. This
          consent can be revoked at any time by contacting us at <a
            href="mailto:privacy@air360.io"
            class="text-blue-600 underline">privacy@air360.io</a
          > or by using the unsubscribe link included in the communications.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          In certain circumstances, where you do not provide Personal information, which is
          required, we will not be able to provide the services and there is a chance you may not be
          able to comply with a legal obligation on us. We will make it clear if and when this
          situation arises and what the consequences of not providing the Personal information would
          be.
        </p>

        {/* Privacy Notice to California Residents */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">
          Privacy Notice to California Residents
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          If you are a resident of California, California Civil Code Section 1798.83 permits you to
          request information regarding the disclosure of your personal information by Air360, Inc
          or its subsidiaries to a third party for the third party’s direct marketing purposes. This
          right granted to California residents applies only to their activities within the State of
          California. To make such a request, please click <a
            href="mailto:privacy@air360.io"
            class="text-blue-600 underline">privacy@air360.io</a
          >. In your request, please specify the name of the partner whose name and/or logo appears
          on this website to which your request pertains. If no company is specified, we will treat
          your request as pertaining to Air360, Inc.
        </p>

        {/* How do you secure my personal information? */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">
          How do you secure my personal information?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We are committed to keeping personal information secure. We have implemented physical,
          technical and administrative safeguards reasonably designed to protect your Personal
          information from unauthorized access and disclosure. When we collect or process Personal
          information, we use industry best standard methods to protect that information. It is
          important that you understand, however, that no website, database or system is completely
          secure or “hacker proof.” You are also responsible for taking reasonable steps to protect
          your personal information against unauthorized disclosure or misuse, for example, by
          protecting your password.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Different countries have different privacy laws and requirements. Please know, however,
          that no matter where your personal information is collected, used, transferred or stored,
          if it was collected through this website, it will be protected by us in accordance with
          the terms of this Privacy Policy and applicable laws, rules and regulations.
        </p>

        {/* Do we share your Personal Information? */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">
          Do we share your Personal Information?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          No (except with some subcontractor with whom we have entered into a data processing
          agreement complying with the provision of the GDPR) unless required by law.
        </p>

        {/* Do we sell or market your Personal Information? */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">
          Do we sell or market your Personal Information?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">No.</p>

        {/* What are my rights? */}
        <h2 class="mb-2 mt-10 text-xl font-bold text-slate-800">What are my rights?</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          You have certain rights in relation to your personal data. Some of these rights will only
          apply in certain circumstances. If an individual would like to exercise, or discuss, any
          of these rights, he should submit his request in writing or email to and provide
          sufficient information to allow us to understand the scope of the request.
        </p>
        <ul class="mb-6 ml-6 list-disc space-y-3 text-slate-700">
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Access:</span> you are entitled to ask us if we are processing
            your personal data and, if we are, you can request access to your personal data. This enables
            you to receive a copy of the personal data we hold about you and certain other information
            about it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Correction:</span> you are entitled to request that any incomplete
            or inaccurate personal data we hold about you is corrected.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Erasure:</span> you are entitled to ask us to delete or remove
            personal data in certain circumstances. There are also certain exceptions where we may refuse
            a request for erasure, for example, where the personal data is required for compliance with
            law or in connection with claims.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Restriction:</span> you are entitled to ask us to suspend the
            processing of your personal data, for example if you want us to establish its accuracy or
            the reason for processing it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Transfer:</span> you are entitled to request the transfer of
            your personal data to another third party in limited circumstances.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Objection:</span> when we process personal data based on legitimate
            interests (or those of a third party) you may challenge this. However, we may be entitled
            to continue processing personal data based on our compelling legitimate interests or where
            this is relevant to legal claims. You also have the right to object to processing personal
            data for direct marketing purposes.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Automated decisions:</span> you are entitled to contest any automated
            decision made about you where this has a legal or similarly significant effect and ask for
            it to be reconsidered.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold">Supervisory Authority:</span> you also have a right to lodge
            a complaint with a supervisory authority, in particular in the Member State in the European
            Union where you are habitually resident, where you work or where an alleged infringement
            of Data Protection Legislation has taken place.
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="font-semibold"
              >Determine guidelines as to the use of your personal data after your death:</span
            > you have a right to determine guidelines as to the storage, erasure and communication of
            your personal data after your death. These guidelines may be general or specific.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
